          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is stained concrete slippery when wet?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The stain itself does not change traction, but the sealer over it can. A glossy film-forming sealer on a smooth slab is genuinely slippery when wet, which matters around pools and on steps. Use a matte or penetrating sealer, or have a slip-resistant additive mixed into the sealer before application.",
